<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      DriverKit dext entitlements. All are RESTRICTED and must be granted by
      Apple (request at developer.apple.com/system-extensions). For local
      development before the grant: `systemextensionsctl developer on` + SIP
      disabled inside the test VM lets you self-assert these.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.driverkit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.developer.driverkit.family.scsicontroller</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      MUST BE REPLACED BEFORE BACKEND B SHIPS.

      This does NOT mean "allow the daemon (by bundle id)", which is what the
      comment here used to claim. It means what it says: it removes the
      requirement that an opener hold `userclient-access` naming this dext, so
      *any* process can IOServiceOpen us. Neither iSCSIUserClient::Start nor
      ExternalMethod checks the caller, and the selectors behind them publish
      LUN geometry, dequeue and complete SCSI tasks, and map the shared payload
      arena — i.e. read/write access to in-flight disk buffers.

      Not live: the dext is excluded from the shipping bundle (see project.yml),
      lives in its own dev scheme, and these entitlements are Apple-approval
      gated. Left alone deliberately rather than fixed blind, because changing
      it means re-requesting the grant and re-testing a parked backend.

      The fix is the paired model: drop this, give iscsid
      `com.apple.developer.driverkit.userclient-access` naming
      me.herko.iSCSIInitiator.dext, and add an explicit client check in Start.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.driverkit.allow-any-userclient-access</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
